```cpp
#include <iostream>
int main() {
int turns = 3;
while (turns > 0) {
    std::cout << turns << "\n";
    turns = turns - 1;
}
std::cout << "Done" << "\n";
    return 0;
}
```

The program prints 3, 2, 1, then Done on separate lines. At zero, it leaves the loop and runs the next statement.
